※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none

※ A store made by a function inlined into one that is inlined in turn.
※
※ `set` is inlined into `fwd` first, callees going first, and `fwd` into `main`
※ after it.  What follows the call to `set` in `fwd` takes no token of its own --
※ every way out of the copy hands on one -- so the token in force there, and at
※ `fwd`'s `ret`, is the one a block above it ended on.  Finding it means looking
※ up the dominator tree, not only in the block: the store of 9 was otherwise
※ hung off the start of the chain, and the read of `x` after it folded into the
※ read before.

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[impure]
fn set(p: &mut u32, v: u32):
    p⌖ ← v

@[impure]
fn fwd(p: &mut u32, v: u32):
    set(p, v)

@[startup, impure]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    let x: mut u32 = 1u32
    set(&mut x, 5u32)
    let a: u32 = x
    fwd(&mut x, 9u32)
    if a = 5u32 ∧ x = 9u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
